BT /F1 9.00 Tf 0.09 0.13 0.20 rg 48.00 765.89 Td (The document makes five major points.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.00 Tf 0.09 0.13 0.20 rg 48.00 746.19 Td (First, one shared agent runtime. This means Stoquify needs one internal control plane for) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.00 Tf 0.09 0.13 0.20 rg 48.00 733.49 Td (all agents, not one framework per module. This is directly aligned with the existing) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.00 Tf 0.09 0.13 0.20 rg 48.00 720.79 Td (architecture. The codebase already centralizes action protection in) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.00 Tf 0.09 0.13 0.20 rg 48.00 708.09 Td (services/_shared/protect.ts, module entitlement in services/modules, RBAC in lib/security,) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.00 Tf 0.09 0.13 0.20 rg 48.00 695.39 Td (snapshots in services/snapshots, and business signals in services/signals. The agent runtime) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.00 Tf 0.09 0.13 0.20 rg 48.00 682.69 Td (should follow that same pattern.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.00 Tf 0.09 0.13 0.20 rg 48.00 662.99 Td (Second, TypeScript-native building blocks. Stoquify is already a Next.js, TypeScript, Prisma) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.00 Tf 0.09 0.13 0.20 rg 48.00 650.29 Td (system. The agent layer should be a TypeScript application concern, not a Python sidecar) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.00 Tf 0.09 0.13 0.20 rg 48.00 637.59 Td (that gradually becomes a parallel product. The external research supports this: the AI SDK) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.00 Tf 0.09 0.13 0.20 rg 48.00 624.89 Td (is now explicitly positioned for TypeScript agent work, tool calling, approvals, runtime) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.00 Tf 0.09 0.13 0.20 rg 48.00 612.19 Td (context, MCP Apps, telemetry, and durability. That fits Stoquify's stack better than) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.00 Tf 0.09 0.13 0.20 rg 48.00 599.49 Td (adopting a large Python-first agent framework.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.00 Tf 0.09 0.13 0.20 rg 48.00 579.79 Td (Third, Stoquify-native domain skills. This is the most important strategic insight. Generic) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.00 Tf 0.09 0.13 0.20 rg 48.00 567.09 Td (frameworks can provide model calls, tool schemas, execution loops, and traces. They cannot) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.00 Tf 0.09 0.13 0.20 rg 48.00 554.39 Td (provide Stoquify's defensibility: tenant-scoped business truth, OHADA/SYSCOHADA context,) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.00 Tf 0.09 0.13 0.20 rg 48.00 541.69 Td (RBAC, evidence grades, source hashes, stock-to-cash-to-close continuity, payroll redaction,) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.00 Tf 0.09 0.13 0.20 rg 48.00 528.99 Td (close assurance, and controlled workflow execution. Those must remain Stoquify-owned.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.00 Tf 0.09 0.13 0.20 rg 48.00 509.29 Td (Fourth, launch three user-facing agents first. The Command Agent, Cash/Reconciliation Agent,) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.00 Tf 0.09 0.13 0.20 rg 48.00 496.59 Td (and Inventory/Replenishment Agent are the right starting set because they meet frequent) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.00 Tf 0.09 0.13 0.20 rg 48.00 483.89 Td (operational needs and can reuse existing read models. They also avoid the highest-risk) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.00 Tf 0.09 0.13 0.20 rg 48.00 471.19 Td (initial domains: statutory filing, ledger posting, close certification, payroll approval,) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.00 Tf 0.09 0.13 0.20 rg 48.00 458.49 Td (and permission changes.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.00 Tf 0.09 0.13 0.20 rg 48.00 438.79 Td (Fifth, no direct dangerous authority. This is non-negotiable. The proposal is valuable) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.00 Tf 0.09 0.13 0.20 rg 48.00 426.09 Td (because agents explain, recommend, draft, and route actions. It becomes dangerous if agents) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.00 Tf 0.09 0.13 0.20 rg 48.00 413.39 Td (directly mutate business records, post ledgers, approve payroll, certify close packs, file) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.00 Tf 0.09 0.13 0.20 rg 48.00 400.69 Td (statutory documents, or change permissions.) Tj ET
